  {
    "_id": "P202",
    "course": "RS102",
    "type": "QUESTION",
    "summary": "What is the difference between the lift coefficient and the lift force?",
    "details": "<p>HW1 asks for both CL and L. Aren't they the same thing?</p>",
    "folders": [
      "RS102-hw1"
    ],
    "author": "567",
    "visibility": "CLASS",
    "visibleTo": [],
    "createdAt": "2026-11-12T14:05:00",
    "views": 9,
    "viewedBy": [
      "567",
      "789",
      "234"
    ],
    "readBy": [
      "567",
      "789",
      "234"
    ],
    "studentAnswers": [
      {
        "_id": "A201",
        "author": "234",
        "createdAt": "2026-11-12T16:40:00",
        "content": "<p>CL describes how good the wing shape is at making lift. The actual force L also depends on how fast you fly and how big the wing is.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "instructorAnswers": [
      {
        "_id": "A202",
        "author": "890",
        "createdAt": "2026-11-12T17:10:00",
        "content": "<p>CL is dimensionless: CL = L / (½ · ρ · V² · S). Multiply it back by the dynamic pressure and the wing area to get the lift force L in newtons.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "discussions": []
  },
